course: dictionary
lesson: 827
title: Belong
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: The word belong has four main meanings. If something belongs to someone, they own it: «Sardinia belongs to Italy» tells you Italy owns it. If something belongs to a group, it is a member of that group or a part of it.
explain: Belong can also mean that something is in the right place. «At the end of a lesson, put books, pencils and papers back where they belong» means back in their proper places. Belong can also mean feeling at home and welcome, like «feel like you belong».
explain: Use the words around belong to choose its meaning. If the sentence is about owning something, pick the meaning about owners. If it is about a group or a set, pick the meaning about membership. Then swap your meaning into the sentence to check it still makes sense.
fact: To belong to someone means to be owned by them.
fact: To belong to a group means to be a member of it.
fact: To belong is to be in the right place, as in «The milk belongs in the fridge.»
fact: «Belongings» means the things you own.
fact: Belong changes its form: belongs, belonged and belonging.
exercise: «Corsica belongs to France.» What does belongs to mean here? | Is painted in France's colours | Is close to France | Is the same size as France | *Is owned by France
exercise: «The milk belongs in the fridge.» What does belongs mean here? | Is very cold | *Is in the right place | Is a member of a club | Is being sold in a shop
exercise: «Put your belongings in the box.» Find and copy one word that means the things you own. | *belongings | your | box | Put
test: «Chalk drawings belong on your own driveway or a quiet path, never on the road.» What does belong mean here? | Are owned by the road | Are wet from the rain | Are a group of cars | *Should be in the right place
test: Which phrase means you feel at home and welcome? | local dialect | *feel like you belong | belongings | wishing fountain
exam: Ella says belong always means own. Is she right? | Yes, and it is a Scottish word | No, it means very old | *No, it can also mean a member of a group, the right place, or feeling at home | Yes, belong only ever means owned by someone
